      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"market for ideas\" theory, championed by John Stuart Mill, posits that the best truth will naturally rise to the top through the open competition of opinions. When the government regulates, it invariably favors one side, effectively proscribing \"unpopular but true\" views, which are crucial for challenging established dogma. This intervention, in this view, not only stifles the necessary \"strong opinion debate\" but also corrupts the very process of truth-seeking, favoring political consensus over intellectual rigor.",
