      "content": "makes sense. so basically even if someone thinks they're regulating to stop \"misinformation,\" they're actually just using their power to control the narrative and silence anyone who disagrees with the state's version of reality. is there any real philosophical way to argue that government moderation is actually \"good\" or is it always just a tool for censorship?",
